    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d307">

                <pb facs="0436" n="356" xml:id="pg356"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Mr.
                            Squiers</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-08-30"><hi rendition="#italic">August 30,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 79.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In reply to your No. 119, of the 22d
                    instant, I have to say that your suggestion to the foreign office that the
                    secretary of your legation, who had been summoned to give evidence in the court
                    of first instance at Habana, could make his deposition at the legation, was in
                    accordance with established precedent, and satisfactory.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
